<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">The main differences between the gauss-newton and the newton method is, that the gauss-newton uses an approximated Hessian, whereas the newton-raphson uses the full Hessian. Regularly, the full term is <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>, but when using the gauss-newton method, only the first term is used: <Equation executable="false" style="2D Math" input-equation="" display=""></Equation>making approximations faster, and when near a solution, f_i(x) becomes so small it can be neglected anyway. </Text-field>
