<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">For which the gradient can be calculated. </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
<Group view="presentation" inline-output="false" labelreference="L507" drawlabel="true" applyint="true" applyrational="true" applyexponent="false">
<Input><Text-field style="Text" layout="Normal">With a deep network and many features, the gradient for each node can be computationally hard. Therefore, backpropagation using the chain rule is utilized. It works by a forward pass through the entire system, computing the prediction. By comparing this with the true value, a backward pass can be made, calculate how much each weight contributed to the error, by applying the chain rule. Lastly, the weights should be adjusted to compensate. Each of  these training loops are called &quot;epochs&quot;. </Text-field>
</Input>
</Group></Presentation-Block><Presentation-Block>
